{
  "name": "giant_octopus",
  "version": 1,
  "introduced_by": "ribshore",
  "notes": "creep: Giant Pacific octopus: brick red, mottled, three and a half metres across the arms. Lies on the sea floor with its arms let down over a rock or a fallen rib, creeps from one high spot to the next, and pales toward the colour of the sand as you swim near; pressed too hard, it jets off backwards with its arms streaming behind.",
